  "term": "BPS",
  "definition": "BPS stands for Battered Person’s Syndrome, a pattern of psychological symptoms seen in people who have experienced intimate partner violence. In forensic mental health, it may be considered when evaluating self-defence claims in cases where a battered person killed the abuser.",
